Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that the sub-units using two types of RNA are major components of the unit consisting of ribosomal protein. Evidence supports that ribosomes are composed of ribosomal RNA (rRNA) and ribosomal proteins, with rRNA forming 60% and ribosomal proteins forming 40%. Additionally, rRNA binds to ribosomal proteins to form functional subunits, and mRNA is decoded by the ribosome during protein synthesis. These findings collectively establish the claim without contradiction.
Rounds: 3, findings: 6
Sources:
- Ribosomal RNA, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribosomal_RNA
- Ribosome, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribosome
